\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- Contribution (1) is the one most exposed by this thesis's own results.}{11}{annotation.1}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}\textbf {GREY AREA} --- Is connectome topology informative, or a lossy re-encoding of the node features?}{15}{annotation.2}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}\textbf {RESEARCH GAP} --- The message-aggregation critique has never been tested in the longitudinal, small-$N$ clinical regime.}{15}{annotation.3}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- Every results table in this thesis is anchored against explicit floors.}{16}{annotation.4}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}\textbf {RESEARCH GAP} --- Same-seed replicate variance is not reported anywhere in the brain-graph literature.}{16}{annotation.5}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- The pipeline developed here is bit-reproducible; the audited baseline is not.}{16}{annotation.6}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}\textbf {RESEARCH GAP} --- No convention exists for constructing AUC-versus-visit-count curves, and the two common constructions can yield opposite conclusions on identical runs.}{17}{annotation.7}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- The follow-up-duration confound is measured, decomposed, and refuted, not assumed away.}{18}{annotation.8}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}\textbf {GREY AREA} --- Whether reconstruction pretraining transfers to clinical discrimination is assumed, not demonstrated.}{18}{annotation.9}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}\textbf {RESEARCH GAP} --- Harmonising visit-time semantics across cohorts is treated as preprocessing bookkeeping, but it is the canonical train-uniform / test-irregular fairness failure.}{19}{annotation.10}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- The held-out test set contains 34 subjects, 14 of them converters.}{20}{annotation.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- The time-awareness of the model cannot be demonstrated on DELCODE, because DELCODE has almost no time variation to be aware of.}{21}{annotation.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}\textbf {RESEARCH GAP} --- Time-aware sequence models are routinely proposed and evaluated on protocol-driven cohorts whose follow-up is regular by design.}{22}{annotation.13}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- Both external cohorts encode \emph {actual elapsed days} rather than scheduled visit labels.}{22}{annotation.14}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {15}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- Naively reusing the DELCODE visit parser on these cohorts fails silently.}{22}{annotation.15}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- Counting artifacts of the filesystem is not the same as counting data --- a lesson learned twice.}{23}{annotation.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {17}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- Leakage prevention here is executable and fails loudly, rather than being described.}{25}{annotation.17}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}\textbf {GREY AREA} --- The standard FC-graph construction gives the message-passing layer strictly less information than the node features it operates on.}{27}{annotation.18}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {19}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- The ablation's interpretation table was pre-registered.}{29}{annotation.19}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {20}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- GEC's explicit visit-count mask is the one place a length shortcut could enter.}{30}{annotation.20}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {21}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- The survival extension is scoped, not delivered, and this thesis says so rather than implying otherwise.}{31}{annotation.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {22}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- Reporting a win over the as-released configuration would be a null comparison.}{33}{annotation.22}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {23}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- Reproducibility itself is a reportable result of this comparison.}{35}{annotation.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {24}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- The determinism of this thesis's \emph {frozen-encoder} arm is asserted from the \texttt {none} arm, not measured directly.}{35}{annotation.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {25}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- An earlier version of this comparison quoted one run per seed out of seven available on disk.}{35}{annotation.25}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {26}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- Brain-TokenGT received no search over its own structural hyperparameters.}{37}{annotation.26}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {27}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- The static GEC classifier currently outscores every recurrent model on this cohort, and the thesis must confront that rather than table it.}{39}{annotation.27}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {28}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- The current fine-tuning conclusion is withdrawn, not merely caveated.}{40}{annotation.28}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {29}\textbf {EXPOSURE} --- Interpretability of an encoder whose contribution is unproven needs framing, not suppression.}{41}{annotation.29}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {30}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- Stating which planned ablations were not run is part of the result.}{41}{annotation.30}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {31}\textbf {OUR EDGE} --- The reproducibility finding was a consequence of the infrastructure, not of suspicion.}{43}{annotation.31}%
